.page readlink 1 print where a symbolic link points

# SYNOPSIS
*readlink* _LINK_...

# DESCRIPTION
`readlink` prints the target of each symbolic link. Something that is not a link produces no output and makes the exit status 1. Words that start with a dash are ignored.

# EXAMPLES
    readlink /usr
    readlink /etc

# SEE ALSO
ln(1), realpath(1), ls(1)
